\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: S. Korea Won Climbs On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 1997\par 23:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Late in global trading, the U.N. unanimously voted to condemn Iraq for its decision to expel Americans from a U.N. weapons inspection team and slap a ban on Iraqi officials who obstruct them. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was probably also pushed higher against both the yen and the mark by short-covering, after some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders braced for steep sell-offs in U.S. stocks after European equities tumbled. \par \par \uc2  'The New York market came in thinking the same thing,' said WestDeutsche Landesbank's Schmelzer-Alicea. 'Everything is going to hell in a hand basket' after falls in Japan's Nikkei 225 stock index and Hong Kong's Hang Seng, 'so the market was actually short dollars.' \par \par \uc2  Although the benchmark Dow Jones Industrial Average fell at its opening it later regained ground before tumbling over 2% late in New York trading. \par \par \uc2  Amid the equity turmoil, sentiment on exotic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was mixed. \par \par \uc2  Many market participants continue to monitor both Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the South Korean won. \par \par \uc2  Although Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in narrow ranges, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of Korea (BOK), \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the won higher against the dollar, according to traders. \par \par \uc2  The BOK was reported to have entered the market at Wednesday's open, selling dollars at 989 won. Late in New York, the dollar was trading at 988.60 won, down slightly from 989.80 won late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah fell against the dollar in mostly technical trading. Late in New York, the dollar was trading at 3,450 rupiah up from Tuesday's Asia close of 3,330 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-11-97 \par \par \uc2  2221GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 20714 4164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbc08o1l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
