\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Korea/989 Won -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Right At Open \b0\par\par\uc2 141 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 1997\par 01:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SEOUL (AP-Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of Korea, entered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade at Wednesday's open, selling dollars at 989 won in an effort to prop up the won, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Right at the session's open, the BOK sold an undetermined amount of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 989 won, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0037 GMT (7:37 p.m. EST), the dollar fell to 985.50 won as a result of the dollar selling. \par \par \uc2  'Looks like the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to make a firm stand at the start of the session to ward off any strong selling pressure on the won today,' a local trader said. \par \par \uc2  -By Cecilia Kang; 822-732-2165; ckang@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0048GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbc08mpd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
