\par\par \b \uc2  S. Korean Won Ends -2: BOK Defends Won AT 999 Won/Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1997\par 09:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SEOUL (AP-Dow Jones)--Despite repeated dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank of Korea, throughout the day, the Korean won settled down 1.9% versus the U.S. dollar Monday, on the Japanese yen's recent depreciation against its major counterparts, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 999 won, up from 985 won at the session's open, and up from 979.90 won at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  Despite repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the morning and afternoon sessions, the dollar maintained its steady climb to the key resistance level of 999 won. \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked determined to keep the won above 999 won per dollar during the day,' said a local dealer. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an undetermined amount of dollars several times throughout the day to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling below 999 won, according to dealers. \par \par \uc2  One dealers said the amount of dollars sold by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its bid to slow the won's sharp pace of depreciation wasn't particularly large. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall versus its major counterparts in recent days puts strong pressure on the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The pressure on Japanese share prices and the general bearishness toward the Japanese economy has pushed the yen lower against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Around 0743 GMT (3:43 a.m. EST), the dollar was trading at Y124, compared with Y123.75 late Friday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's moves against the won often mirror the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade versus the yen as Korean exporters vie for price competitiveness of their products compared with Japanese products. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, continued bearishness toward the stability of the country's financial sector, vulnerable to more bankruptcies, according to analysts, pushed the won lower. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar is expected to trade at an average rate of 997 won Tuesday,\par compared with its average trading rate of 979.40 won Monday.\par -By Cecilia Kang; 822-732-2165; ckang@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-11-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0808GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1063 1858 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtba08i4d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
