\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  woes push down Singapore stocks. \b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 7 (Reuters) - Asia's bumpy road to recovery and the worsening health of the South Korean won returned to trample the Singapore stock market and other regional bourses on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Nearly every major stock market in Asia fell. People are very nervous and talking of a second wave of selling in Hong Kong soon. All these because the region remains fragile, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weak and maybe this is really the beginning," said a dealer with a local house. \par \par \uc2  After opening at 1,691.82, the Straits Times Industrials Index ended at 1,671.25, down 19.28 points or 1.14 percent. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the won posted another record-low close of 979.9 despite two \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fuelling fears \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be the next candidate for the International Monetary Fund aid. \par \par \uc2  The won's fall sent some Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  reeling and regional stock markets in Tokyo, Hong Kong and Taiwan tumbling. \par \par \uc2  Property counters led the drop in Singapore's stock market, with the index plunging 21.50 points, or 4.95 percent, to 412.85. \par \par \uc2  Sharp drops were noted in property heavyweights. First Capital tumbled 90 cents to S$2.86, City Development shed 40 cents to S$7.05 and Singapore Land dropped 32 cents to S$4.28. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the property companies were hit after reports that bids for a well-located residential site in Singapore were 25 to 30 percent below expectations. \par \par \uc2  Real estate firm Colliers Jardine called it the weakest tender in years. \par \par \uc2  Share trading in electronic parts distributor Electronic Resources Ltd was suspended pending a company announcement. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the company could be a takeover target of U.S.-listed Ingram Micro Inc, the world's biggest computer wholesale distributor. \par \par \uc2  Ingram was rumoured to be keen on securing 24 percent stake in ERL at S$2.10 per share. \par \par \uc2  Selective electronic shares bucked the market downtrend. \par \par \uc2  Led by a S$1.10 rise in multimedia Creative Technology to S$44.30, the SES electronic index rose 0.42 percent to 140.36. \par \par \uc2  "The outlook for the electronic sector is bright ahead of the year-end festive demand. Creative is expected to do well in terms of its order book," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  -- Angela Tan (65) 870-3083; Fax (65) 776-8112 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: singapore.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb702xgf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
