\par\par \b \uc2  S. Korean Won Lower Early On Yen Fall Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 1997\par 02:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SEOUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The South Korean won is lower early Thursday, despite the Bank of Korea's dollar selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  minutes after the session began, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0101 GMT (8:01 p.m. EST), the dollar was trading at 974 won, compared with 969.70 won at Wednesday's close. The dollar opened Thursday at 970 won. \par \par \uc2  As reported, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade early Thursday, selling dollars in a bid to support the won, which was depreciating quickly, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0040 GMT (7:40 p.m. EST), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an undetermined amount of spot dollars at 975 won. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar' sharp rise against the Japanese yen in global trade boosted the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the won in Korea,' said a dealer at SeoulBank. \par \par \uc2  Amid Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil, traders believe the Japan, which send a large percentage of its exports to regional countries, will suffer from lower demand. In addition, Japan's financial stability was again put in doubt after the bankruptcy of brokerage Sanyo Securities, which fueled fears of more financial companies failing, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0101 GMT (8:01 p.m. EST), the dollar was trading at Y123.10, up from Y123.07 in New York late Wednesday, and up from Y122.05 late in Tokyo Wednesday. The last time the dollar was stronger against the yen was on May 9, when it reached Y123.71. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's moves versus the yen are often tracked by the dollar's trade against the won as Korean exporters compete for more attractive export prices versus their Japanese rivals. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to continue supporting the won throughout the session, which should hamper further gains of the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By Cecilia Kang; 822-732-2165; ckang@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0116GMT \par \par \uc2  1063 1858 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtb608fg8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
