\par\par \b \uc2  S. Korea  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\uc2  To Sell Dollars \b0\par\par\uc2 134 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 1997\par 09:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SEOUL (AP-Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times to sell the dollar in the market Friday near 909 won in its attempt to halt a rapid fall of the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  According to the dealers, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars between 908.90 won and 909 won. However, the amount of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold by the Bank of Korea wasn't immediately available. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a seller of the dollar recently to slow down the rapid gain of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spurred by jitters of a credit crunch from recent bankruptcies and financial woes at major South Korean conglomerates. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-09-97 \par \par \uc2  0747GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9c06t87\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
