\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Korea sells dlrs in 4th  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 134 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Aug 25 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of Korea, sold dollars at 904.00 won in early Monday afternoon in its fourth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the day in the interbank market to slow the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  After the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the won rebounded to as high as 902.50 after hitting an all-time low of 904.10 early in the afternoon session. \par \par \uc2  The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times in the morning session, once in the spot and twice in the forward trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the won was pressured by strong dollar demand in line with the dollar shortages at local merchant banks in the aftermath of corporate debt defaults. \par \par \uc2  -- Seoul newsroom (822) 727 5646 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8p00tnf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
