\par\par \b \uc2  S. Korea Won Ends Slightly Higher On Trade Surplus \b0\par\par\uc2 231 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1997\par 10:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SEOUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The South Korean won ended slightly higher Wednesday on expectations the country would continue to post a trade surplus toward the end of this year, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 887.20 won, compared to 887.80 won Tuesday, they said. \par \par \uc2  After opening at 887.60 won, the dollar moved in a tight range, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'Selling pressure on the dollar was pretty heavy because of the trade deficit in June,' a local trader said. 'The market also appears to be in a dollar overbought position.' \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the government said the country swung to a trade surplus of $98 million last month from a deficit of $426 million a year ago, led by exports of South Korea's major export items, such as semiconductors and petrochemical goods. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Bank of Thailand's surprise decision to float the Thai baht had no impact on the local stock market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Thailand announced it would institute a 'managed float' of the baht. \par \par \uc2  'If (\b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's) \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar at 887.00 won, the U.S. dollar may fall to 886.00 won,' another dealer at a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0822GMT \par \par \uc2  1063 1858 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7204wbl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picw