\par\par \b \uc2  S. Korean Won Higher Early After Central Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 1997\par 02:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SEOUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The South Korean won is higher early Thursday, boosted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  right after the market's open, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0054 GMT, the dollar was trading at 868.20 won, compared with 869.50 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea (BOK), \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday, right after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened at the key resistance level of 870 won, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'They \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 870 won,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a local bank. 'And they probably will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout the day at that level,' the trader said. \par \par \uc2  Right after the BOK's dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar fell to its intraday low of 868.50 won. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said it is unclear how much of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the BOK sold in early trading. \par \par \uc2  Strong dollar demand off of the dollar's strength in global markets pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the key resistance level of 870 won at the session's open, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Also weighing on the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the country's burdensome trade deficit, which widened to $3.48 billion in January, from a shortfall of $2.13 billion in the same period in 1996. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the dollar to again test key resistance of 870 won in the session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-02-97 \par \par \uc2  0103GMT \par \par \uc2  1063 1858 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2600raq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
