\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -4:  \highlight22\uc2 South Korea Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Again \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1997\par 23:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  During Asian trading, the dollar softened slightly after the president of Toyota Motor Corp. said a dollar between 100 to 110 yen is 'appropriate.' \par \par \uc2  Hiroshi Okuda said Japanese automakers wouldn't be able to book profits and thereby have funds for capital spending if the dollar falls to 95 yen. \par \par \uc2  Also in Tokyo, the director-general of Japan's Economic Planning Agency (EPA) said that Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka acknowledged the stock market's concerns that the country's economy will weaken after April and that the government isn't serious about reform. \par \par \uc2  The EPA director quoted Mitsuzuka as saying swift implementation of a budget for the next fiscal year beginning April 1 as well as structural reform are necessary to stop the stock market's decline. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Chief Cabinet Secretary Seiroku Kajiyama said the government will promptly implement a series of promised reforms to calm jitters over the stock market. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the Nikkei average of 225 selected issues declined almost 11%. Since then, it, has retraced some losses although questions remain over just how stable Japanese stocks will be. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again stepped into local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem the decline of the won, making \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seem almost like a daily ritual. \par \par \uc2  Since the end of 1996, the Bank of Korea (BOK) has vigorously been in the market to curb the won's depreciation against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The BOK sold dollars between 848.10 won and 848.60 won at least three times Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Late in Seoul, the dollar was at 848.50 won, up from 846.60 won. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-01-97 \par \par \uc2  2249GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1e00c3s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
