\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: U.K. Minutes Stoke Rate Rise Chance \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 1996\par 22:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar was at 1.3370 Swiss francs, up from 1.3345 francs. The mark was at 982.31 lire, down from 984.21 lire. \par \par \uc2  Dealers hesitated to attribute the mark's two-lira swing during global trading to much more than investors squaring up their portfolios. \par \par \uc2  'These are not real markets. I don't think anyone should be too concerned,' with the mark's moves, said Jay Wertheimer, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader, Banco Di Sicilia in New York. \par \par \uc2  Dealers did, however, find reason to buy sterling after the release of the minutes of the October 30 monetary meeting between Bank of England Governor Eddie George and Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke. \par \par \uc2  George warned a 0.25 percentage point rise in the base lending rate 'might well not be enough' to meet the government's inflation target for the next two years. \par \par \uc2  'It confirmed market expectations that the 25 basis point hike may even be too small for the longer term,' said MTB's Katz. Britain's 'economy continues to show signs of strength and interest rate expectations are' up. \par \par \uc2  The meeting between George and Clarke was the last time the base rate was raised to 6% from 5.75%. \par \par \uc2  The government has set a target for underlying inflation, which excludes mortgage interest payments, of 2.5% or below before the next election which must be held by the end of May 1997. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, sterling was at 2.6092 marks, up from 2.5941 marks. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vigorously \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local markets, selling $400 million for won to keep the won from hitting a six-year low. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-12-96 \par \par \uc2  2159GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dscn020ch\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
