\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: S. Korea Won Dn Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 1996\par 23:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Australian Treasurer Peter Costello said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to cut rates is 'terrific' news for the economy and called on major banks to pass on the cut to home buyers immediately. \par \par \uc2  Heeding his call, four major Australian commercial banks dropped their home loan rates after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister John Howard also said the government will continue to pursue a strategy promoting sustained economic and employment growth in 1997. \par \par \uc2  The prime minister said government policies are working, as evidenced by Australia's low inflation environment and consequent downward pressure on interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The officials 'saw enough flexibility to move the market now. If the economy should expand a little bit next year, then they've been right on course,' said Sakamoto. 'If they cut now, they can see the results earlier. If economic recovery doesn't pick up, they can cut again next year. If it does pick up, they can always raise rates.' \par \par \uc2  In fact, some market players don't dismiss the possibility of another Australian rate cut, although it probably won't happen again this year. Wednesday morning's cut marks the third easing this year. \par \par \uc2  The cash rate is the rate on funds lent overnight between banks and other institutions. It was last lowered Nov. 6 from 7.0% to 6.5%. \par \par \uc2  After spending two trading sessions at six-year lows, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the won, traders in Seoul said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dropped to 838.85 won from an intraday high of 843 won after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't confirm the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-12-96 \par \par \uc2  2220GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dscb01o24\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
