\par\par \b \uc2  S. Korea Won Again Breaks 6-Yr Lows Despite BOK Dlr Sale \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 1996\par 10:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SEOUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday wasn't enough to hamper the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from breaking, yet again, six-year average, intraday and closing lows, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar closed at 839.30 won Wednesday, sharply higher from Tuesday's ending level of 836.30 won Tuesday - a level last seen before March 1990 when the country's government introduced its current market average system. \par \par \uc2  Also breaching six-year record average and intraday highs Tuesday of 835.20 won and 836.60 won, respectively, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  averaged 839.00 won and peaked to 843.20 won Wednesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Waiting for the Bank of Korea (BOK), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to step in and support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its free fall this week - dropping more than 12 won against the dollar from last week - the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  heeded investors' calls for dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  'The market was waiting for the (BOK) to step in and stop the won from falling further from Tuesday's large losses,' said a trader at a large European bank in Seoul. He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the only force that could prevent the won from losing even further during current seasonal dollar demand. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was said to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Seoul \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading around 0520 GMT Wednesday, selling a modest amount of dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't confirm whether it entered the local markets Wednesday as large dollar sellers. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-12-96 \par \par \uc2  0940GMT \par \par \uc2  1063 1858 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dscb01lph\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
