\par\par \b \uc2  BOK  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to prop up dollars - dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 137 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Aug 3 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of Korea (BOK), \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost U.S. dollars against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the won, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied the speculation, in accordance with its normal policy. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around the 757.60/757.70 level," said a foreign bank dealer. "But I cannot guess how many dollars they bought." \par \par \uc2  The won opened at 757.40 but fell sharply to 758.40 in early morning trading after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "I believe the BOK bought dollars to boost the greenback in line with the dollar's gain in strength against the yen on the world market," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  -- Seoul newsroom (822) 727 5647 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr8305bz0\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (South Korea near10 interven*) 